{"dynamic_request": "Solve the system of equations $ 2a - b = 9 $, $ 2c - d = 3 $, $ a - 3b = 7 $, and $ c - 3d = -1 $ to find the entries of the matrix $ \\mathbf{M} $.", "stage_instruction": "Initialize local reasoning", "selected_context_ids": ["s2", "s1"], "original_question_and_constraints": "A matrix $\\mathbf{M}$ takes $\\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}$ to $\\begin{pmatrix} 9 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix},$ and $\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\end{pmatrix}$ to $\\begin{pmatrix} 7 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}.$  Find the image of the line $y = 2x + 1$ under $\\mathbf{M}.$  Express your answer in the form \"$y = mx + b$\".", "relevant_source_evidence": {}, "anchor_reasoning_context": {"s2": "Let $ \\mathbf{M} = \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \\end{pmatrix} $. Then, using the given transformations, we have the following equations: $ 2a - b = 9 $, $ 2c - d = 3 $, $ a - 3b = 7 $, and $ c - 3d = -1 $. Solving these equations will give us the values of $ a, b, c, $ and $ d $, which define the matrix $ \\mathbf{M} $.", "s1": "To find the image of the line $ y = 2x + 1 $ under the matrix $ \\mathbf{M} $, we first need to determine the matrix $ \\mathbf{M} $ itself. We are given two vectors and their images under $ \\mathbf{M} $: $ \\mathbf{v}_1 = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} \rightarrow \\mathbf{Mv}_1 = \begin{pmatrix} 9 \\ 3 \\end{pmatrix} $ and $ \\mathbf{v}_2 = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -3 \\end{pmatrix} \rightarrow \\mathbf{Mv}_2 = \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} $. Using these, we can set up a system of equations to solve for the entries of $ \\mathbf{M} $."}, "max_total_output_tokens": 512, "max_draft_tokens": 384, "previous_private_outputs": []}

